From: TrailCurrent
Subject: [PATCH] gobex: Do not crash when the transport closes during a read

g_io_channel_read_chars() returns G_IO_STATUS_EOF without setting an error
when the remote closes the connection, and read_packet() then dereferenced
the NULL error to build its own message. A phone dropping its PBAP
connection mid-transfer crashed obexd. Report the closed transport instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/gobex/gobex.c
+++ b/gobex/gobex.c
@@ -1301,9 +1301,12 @@
 	status = g_io_channel_read_chars(io, (char *) obex->rx_buf,
 					obex->rx_mtu, &rbytes, &read_err);
 	if (status != G_IO_STATUS_NORMAL) {
+		/* EOF (the remote closed the transport) comes without an error */
 		g_set_error(err, G_OBEX_ERROR, G_OBEX_ERROR_PARSE_ERROR,
-				"Unable to read data: %s", read_err->message);
-		g_error_free(read_err);
+				"Unable to read data: %s",
+				read_err ? read_err->message : "transport closed");
+		if (read_err)
+			g_error_free(read_err);
 		goto fail;
 	}
 
